  "term": "polysomnography",
  "definition": "Polysomnography is a sleep study that continuously records several body functions at the same time during sleep to examine normal and disturbed sleep. It typically tracks brain activity to identify sleep stages along with measures such as breathing, eye movements, and blood oxygen levels.",
